From e87fd30464c6893672669dca3c686eff240e25fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:13:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos7870-gtaxlwifi: run the eMMC in HS200

The card declares HS200 (DEVICE_TYPE 0x57) and vqmmc is already at 1.8 V;
the CIU reaches 799.5 MHz from bus_pll/2, which with ciu-div = 3 gives
199.875 MHz on the bus, the same 800 MHz CIU clock the vendor kernel
used. Tuning finds a sample phase on every boot. Measured sequential
reads go from 53-81 MB/s in DDR52 to 58-158 MB/s (median ~115), and two
full reads of the 3.1 GB super partition hash identically.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
index 53ccbf3a52..a367876f55 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
@@ -1375,8 +1375,15 @@ &mmc0 {
 	 * HS200/HS400 sono un passo separato: vogliono mmc-hs200-1_8v e poi
 	 * mmc-hs400-1_8v + samsung,dw-mshc-hs400-timing + read-strobe-delay,
 	 * con gli stessi vincoli di formato a due celle descritti sotto.
+	 *
+	 * HS200: the card declares it (DEVICE_TYPE 0x57), vqmmc is at 1.8 V,
+	 * and the CIU can reach 799.5 MHz (bus_pll/2), i.e. 199.875 MHz on the
+	 * bus with ciu-div = 3, the same 800 MHz the Samsung kernel asked for
+	 * (clock-frequency). The sample phase comes from the driver's tuning;
+	 * the drive phase is the sdr-timing one.
 	 */
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 
 	/*
 	 * Timing nel formato MAINLINE a due celle: dw_mci_exynos_parse_dt()
-- 
2.47.3

